  "currentRoundInspection": {
    "inspectedOn": "2026-10-15",
    "scope": "Three actually inspected2007/2009 exterior photographs:glass shell and detached spire from two views,plus complete stitched spire detail.No bespoke plans/surveys researched or reference photos/reflections redistributed.Old photos guide exterior form;hidden/current details,height datum and thresholds remain approximate.",
    "pictures": [
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crystal_Cathedral_with_Spire.jpg",
        "author": "Wattewyl",
        "date": "2009-04-12",
        "license": "CC-BY-3.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected northeastern exterior. Broad blue-gray reflective glass planes,thin regular horizontal/vertical rectangular pane grid,sharp high wing tips and an angular inward roof valley. Low pale-framed entrance canopies lie at the base. Separate narrow silver steel spire has many tall pointed blades,visible gaps and stepped tip heights. Roof silhouette and steel/glass proportions guide geometry;reflected sky/trees,cars and incidental landscaping are not baked into the model."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crys-ext.jpg",
        "author": "Arnold C (Buchanan-Hermit);perspective/crop edits by Commons contributors",
        "date": "2007-05-08",
        "license": "Attribution-required free-use permission on Commons",
        "observed": "Actually inspected another full exterior. The pointed glass shell has broad faceted roof/wall planes and a pronounced inward V-like valley between high tips. Fine rectangular pane rows cover roof and walls. Silver detached spire is taller than the cathedral,with narrow open vertical blades and varying pointed crowns. A small pale circular/rounded pavilion with a gold-toned shallow cap is visible within the spire base. Canopies are low pale rectangular frames. Hidden roof joints and exact entrance arrangement remain approximate."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crystal_Cathedral_spire_complete.jpg",
        "author": "Wattewyl",
        "date": "2009-04-12",
        "license": "CC-BY-3.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected complete tall stitched spire photograph. Slim grouped steel blade/prism elements rise to staggered needle points;some blades stop above the ground,leaving a broad open base around the small pale circular pavilion. Repeated dark inner structural/bell rows and narrow connectors show through gaps. No opaque filled tower shaft. Individual bell count,engineering sections and exact blade count/offsets are simplified,not surveyed."
      }
    ]
  }
